`migrate.sh` runs this migration on any Linux or macOS machine that can reach the source database{{if ne .TargetKind "directory"}} and the target cluster{{end}}. It doesn't need the Omni-Data-Bus tool: it carries the mappings and runs the `odb` command-line runner, the same engine as the tool.
{{- if .Plaintext}}

> **Warning:** this export contains the database credentials in plain text. Anyone with
> `migrate.sh` can connect to the source{{if .TargetHasCredentials}} and the target{{end}}. Keep it like a password, and delete it after use.
{{- end}}
{{- if .ConfigFile}}

> **Warning:** `config.json` holds the database credentials. They are base64-encoded, which
> keeps them from being read at a glance but is not encryption: anyone with the file can
> connect to the source{{if .TargetHasCredentials}} and the target{{end}}. Keep it like a password, and delete it after use.
{{- end}}

